SPL -- the print spooler's queue directory==========================================splman (the manager), splprt (the printer process) and splstat (the statusreport) all open /DD/SPL/splq.  Without the directory and the file they eachstopped at error 216, path-not-found, and said nothing.splq is here and EMPTY: an empty queue is the correct state for a spoolerwith nothing to print.THE CLIENTS WANT A MODULE, NOT A FILE.  `lpq', `prjob' and `lp' belongto a second spooler, and look for a DATA MODULE called `spoolqueue' inmemory; they answer `no spooler installed' when it is not there.Starting `splman &' does not create it -- splman runs, as a daemonshould, and lpq still says no spooler.  Measured 2026-08-29.`lpsched' BUILDS IT, and with lpsched running the whole set works.Measured 2026-09-23 on os9exec b5da6df:    lpsched /pipe/prt &   forks prjob and stays resident, waiting in F$Event    edir -e               lists the event `spoolqueue'    lp <file>             Spoolid : 1    lpq                   Defaultprinter: /pipe/prt, and the spool files    lprm 1                No Job to delete -- prjob already has job 1    lpshut                stops the spooler; lpq then says                          `Spooler is not active'Until that day lpq, lpshut and lp still answered `no spooler installed',`no spooler active' and `Spooler not installed' with the queue inmemory: they find it with modlink() asking for a Data module, and theemulator's F$DatMod did not give the module it made that type.  Sourcefor the set is in /dd/SRC/eff_lp.  Name your own printer in place of/pipe/prt.